<% layout("/layouts/boilerplate.ejs") %>

<header class="bg-primary text-white ext-center py-5">
    <div class="container">
        <h1 class="display-4">Gohar Mahal</h1>
        <p class="lead">A symbol of Bhopal’s regal history and Indo-Islamic architecture</p>
    </div>
</header>

<div class="container my-5">
    <img src="https://www.trawell.in/admin/images/upload/145239559Bhopal_Gohar_Mahal_Main.jpg"
        class="hero-img rounded mb-4" alt="Gohar Mahal Bhopal">

    <section>
        <h2>History</h2>
        <p>Gohar Mahal was built in 1820 by Qudsia Begum (also known as Gohar Begum), the first female ruler of Bhopal. It was one of the earliest palaces in the city and a landmark for the beginning of female leadership in Bhopal’s rich history. The palace served as a royal residence and a cultural center during the reign of the Begums.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-4">
        <h2>Geography and Significance</h2>
        <p>Located on the banks of Upper Lake, Gohar Mahal is situated near the heart of old Bhopal. It is a blend of Hindu and Mughal architectural styles, and today stands as a heritage site that reflects the city's progressive and inclusive royal lineage. The palace is a testament to the powerful role of women in Bhopal’s governance.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-4">
        <h2>Activities and Attractions</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Heritage Architecture:</strong> Explore intricate carvings, jharokhas, and ornate doorways.</li>
            <li><strong>Cultural Events:</strong> Hosts art exhibitions, craft fairs, and cultural festivals like the India Craft Week.</li>
            <li><strong>Photography:</strong> Ideal for history buffs and architecture lovers capturing the beauty of heritage design.</li>
            <li><strong>Lakefront View:</strong> Enjoy the scenic view of Upper Lake just outside the palace walls.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-4">
        <h2>Environmental Importance</h2>
        <p>Being adjacent to the Bhojtal (Upper Lake), the palace benefits from a serene natural setting and contributes to the visual and cultural landscape of Bhopal. Preservation efforts help maintain both ecological harmony and historical pride in the region.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-4">
        <h2>Gallery</h2>
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-md-4 mb-3">
                <img width="300" height="300" src="https://tickettolywood.travel.blog/wp-content/uploads/2019/03/803e9-whatsapp2bimage2b2018-06-042bat2b11.57.582bam.jpeg"
                    class="img-fluid rounded" alt="Gohar Mahal Interior">
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-4 mb-3">
                <img width="300" height="300" src="https://encrypted-tbn0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTbm8j2XQHEPCsvwX5xxOyXYQpIqdnUJfQcZQTPbP-KYIQtnml4v2yewSHsIGq11HlGG28&usqp=CAU"
                    class="img-fluid rounded" alt="Front of Gohar Mahal">
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-4 mb-3">
                <img width="300" height="300" src="https://encrypted-tbn0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcQzs6GlRrHMHvDrBfZtG8XaQzRFq11NI6KOxQ-PO3HsGgaQYsIRkbf2Bqua4bfLufDyhLs&usqp=CAU"
                    class="img-fluid rounded" alt="Gohar Mahal Architecture">
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
</div>
 <section class="mt-5">
    <div class="container">
        <h2 class="mb-4">User Reviews</h2>

        <!-- Review Form -->
        <form action="/bhopal/<%= place %>/review" method="POST" id="reviewForm" class="mb-5">
            <div class="row">
                <div class="mb-3 col-12 col-sm-6 col-md-4">
                    <label for="reviewRating" class="form-label">Rating</label>
                    <select name="rating" class="form-select" id="reviewRating" required>
                        <option value="" disabled selected>Select rating</option>
                        <option value="5">⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐ - Excellent</option>
                        <option value="4">⭐⭐⭐⭐ - Very Good</option>
                        <option value="3">⭐⭐⭐ - Good</option>
                        <option value="2">⭐⭐ - Fair</option>
                        <option value="1">⭐ - Poor</option>
                    </select>
                </div>

                <div class="mb-3 col-12">
                    <label for="reviewText" class="form-label">Your Review</label>
                    <textarea name="comment" class="form-control" id="reviewText" rows="4" required></textarea>
                </div>

                <div class="col-12">
                    <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary">Submit Review</button>
                </div>
            </div>
        </form>

        <!-- Reviews List -->
        <div id="reviewsList">
            <% if (reviews.length === 0) { %>
                <p class="text-muted">No reviews yet. Be the first to write one!</p>
            <% } %>
            <div class="row ">
                <% reviews.forEach(review => { %>
                    <div class="singleReview card col-12 col-sm-6 col-lg-3 mb-4 mx-md-1 ">
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <h4 class="card-title"><%= review.author.username %></h4>
                            <p class="card-text"><%= review.comment %></p>
                            <p class="card-text">
                                <%= '⭐'.repeat(review.rating) %> 
                            </p>

                            <!-- Edit and Delete Buttons -->
                            <div class="d-flex justify-content-start">
                                <a href="/bhopal/<%= place %>/review/<%= review._id %>/edit" class="btn btn-outline-primary mx-2">Edit</a>
                                <form method="POST" action="/bhopal/<%= place %>/review/<%= review._id %>?_method=DELETE" >
                                    <button type="submit" class="btn btn-outline-danger">Delete</button>
                                </form>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                <% }) %>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>



